**D = B + 12·d'_B = (5√10/2 + 12√10/8, √6/2 − 36√6/8) = (5√10/2 + 3√10/2, √6/2 − 9√6/2) = (4√10, −4√6)**

Verification via C: D = C + 8·d'_C = (15√10/4 + √10/4, −3√6/4 − 13√6/4) = (4√10, −4√6) ✓

## Computing AD

$$AD = \sqrt{(4\sqrt{10})^2 + (4\sqrt{6})^2} = \sqrt{160 + 96} = \sqrt{256} = 16$$

